@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: permissions the sandbox boundary denies and claudecode reports every run — the auto-updater, whose fix is to STOP trying, and a workspace hook, whose fix is the opposite
' status: proposed 2026-09-10, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: defs/claudecode/harness.manifest (agentEnv)
' would touch: defs/claudecode/tests/ (the assertion opencode already has)
' would touch: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (proveo_install_claude_hooks)
'   what proveo's own hook install does . _spec/internal/sbx/virtiofs-cwd-invalidation.puml
'   how a clone re-materialises modes ... _spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml
'   why the version is pinned at all . _spec/_devops/agent-version-pin.puml
'   the precedent, done properly ..... defs/opencode/Dockerfile (OPENCODE_AUTO_UPDATE)
'   the same shape on cursor ......... _spec/defs/cursor/cursor-paradigm.puml
'   where the flag already appears ... defs/claudecode/mcp/Dockerfile (BUILD only)
'   where it was seen and dismissed .. _spec/internal/sbx/seed-node-version-abort.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
'   THE CLASS THIS IS AN INSTANCE OF: _spec/_paradigms/workspace-boundary.puml
'     — direct mode imports the host's file semantics; a clone re-materialises
'     them. Presence, mode/ownership, architecture and which-tree are one cause
'     meeting four properties of a file. Keep only this file's distinct half.
'
' ── THE SYMPTOM ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Every claudecode run prints:
'
'   ✘ Auto-update failed: no write permission to npm prefix · Run claude doctor
'
' It is not new, and this tree has already met it: seed-node-version-abort.puml
' lists "Claude Code's failing auto-updater" among twelve mechanisms proposed and
' ELIMINATED while bisecting an unrelated abort. So it was looked at, correctly
' ruled out as the cause of that bug, and never fixed as a fault of its own.
'
' ── WHY IT HAPPENS, AND IT IS WORKING AS DESIGNED ──────────────────────────
' The CLI is installed at build time as root; the run is non-root. `proveo-harden`
' strips setuid, the def declares `security.non-root=true`, and nothing grants
' the runtime user write access to the npm prefix — deliberately. So the updater
' finds the prefix unwritable and says so.
'
' The message is also bad advice HERE: `claude doctor` is interactive, and an
' unattended run has nobody to read it.
'
' ── THE FLAG EXISTS AND IS ALREADY SET — IN THE WRONG SCOPE ────────────────
' `DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1` appears in this tree twice, and neither reaches the
' running agent:
'   defs/claudecode/mcp/Dockerfile   sets it for a BUILD step, alongside
'                                    `HOME=/tmp/claude-build` — build hygiene,
'                                    scoped to that RUN and gone afterwards
'   lsp-plugins-seed.puml            cites it, without the def setting it
'
' And claudecode's `agentEnv:` — the runtime env the manifest hands the agent —
' carries only CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_ALTERNATE_SCREEN and CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER.
' The auto-updater is never told to stand down at RUN time. That gap is the
' whole defect: a one-line omission in a file that already does this for two
' other variables.
'
' ── WHY WRITE PERMISSION IS THE WRONG FIX, AND IT IS NOT CLOSE ─────────────
' The obvious repair — make the prefix writable — is worse than the symptom, for
' three independent reasons:
'
'   IT DEFEATS THE PIN. agent-version-pin.puml exists so a run uses the version
'     the image was built with; build.sh resolves CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION and passes
'     it as a build-arg. An updater that SUCCEEDS silently replaces that binary,
'     and the posture line naming the pinned version becomes a lie. A successful
'     update is a worse outcome than a failed one.
'   IT MAKES THE IMAGE AGENT-MUTABLE. Writable global npm means the agent can
'     rewrite its own tooling mid-run, which cuts against the hardened,
'     non-root posture the defs assert in their security tests.
'   IT BUYS NOTHING. The container is ephemeral. A download that succeeds is
'     discarded at teardown, so the cost is paid every run and kept never.
'
' ── THE PRECEDENT IS ALREADY IN THE TREE, DONE PROPERLY ────────────────────
' opencode solved exactly this and left the pattern:
'   defs/opencode/Dockerfile      ENV OPENCODE_AUTO_UPDATE=false — RUNTIME
'   defs/opencode/tests/          test_security.sh asserts the variable, so the
'                                 fix cannot silently regress
'   sample_opencode.json,         "autoupdate": false in the config too, for the
'   defaults/opencode.json        path the env var does not cover
'
' cursor-paradigm.puml records the same shape a third time — "the CLI's runtime
' auto-update cannot write there either" — so this is a class, met three times,
' fixed once. Claudecode should follow opencode: set it in `agentEnv`, and assert
' it, because an unasserted env var is a comment.
'
' ── CASE B · THE WORKSPACE'S OWN STOP HOOK IS DENIED ──────────────────────
' A second permission failure, reported the same way and needing the OPPOSITE
' remedy:
'
'   ● Ran 1 stop hook
'     ⎿ Stop hook error: Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: 1:
'       <workspace>/.claude/hooks/stop-checks.sh: Permission denied
'
' "Its own hooks are denied?" — not its own. That path is the WORKSPACE's hook,
' brought by the repository being worked on, and the distinction is the whole
' diagnosis.
'
' PROVEO GUARANTEES EXEC FOR THE HOOKS IT SHIPS, AND NOTHING FOR THE REST.
' `proveo_install_claude_hooks` installs from `/opt/claudecode/defaults/hooks/
' cwd-guard.sh` — baked into the image, `-rwxr-xr-x`, owned by the runtime user.
' The same is true of `defs/cursor/defaults/hooks/audit-shell.sh`. A hook the
' WORKSPACE carries gets none of that: nothing chmods it, nothing validates it,
' and nothing reports that it will not run until Claude Code tries.
'
' ── WHAT IT IS NOT, MEASURED FROM INSIDE A SANDBOX ────────────────────────
' It is NOT a noexec mount, which is the first guess and is wrong here:
'     host on /Users/pluvo/.proveo type virtiofs (rw,nosuid,nodev,relatime)
' `nosuid` and `nodev`, no `noexec`. virtiofs permits execution.
'
' And a CLONE-mode workspace sidesteps the question entirely: the clone lands on
' an ext4 volume inside the VM, git re-materialises it, and files arrive as
' `-rwxr-xr-x 1 1000 1000` — owned by the runtime user with the exec bit git
' tracked. The failing path is a DIRECT-mode workspace, where the host's own
' modes and ownership arrive through virtiofs untouched.
'
' ── SO IT IS ONE OF TWO THINGS, AND ONE COMMAND SEPARATES THEM ────────────
'   NO EXEC BIT ON THE HOST   git tracks exactly one exec bit, so a hook
'                             committed without it will not run in ANY sandbox,
'                             or on the host either. The most common cause and
'                             the least interesting.
'   UID MISMATCH              the file has +x but a mode that excludes others —
'                             0700 owned by the host user — while the sandbox
'                             runs as uid 1000. Then execve returns EACCES and
'                             /bin/sh prints exactly this line.
'
' On the host:
'     ls -l .claude/hooks/stop-checks.sh; git ls-files -s .claude/hooks/
' Mode `100755` in the index means git carries the bit and the fault is
' ownership; `100644` means the bit was never committed and `chmod +x` plus a
' commit fixes it everywhere at once.
'
' ── AND THE REMEDY IS THE INVERSE OF CASE A, WHICH IS THE POINT ───────────
' These two errors look alike — a permission denial, non-fatal, printed every
' run — and they must not be fixed alike:
'
'   THE AUTO-UPDATER   the operator does NOT want it to succeed. A success
'                      would unpin the image. Remedy: stop it trying.
'   THE WORKSPACE HOOK the operator DOES want it to succeed. They wrote it.
'                      Remedy: make the permission work.
'
' THE RULE THAT SEPARATES THEM: ask whether the operator wants the thing to
' happen. If yes, fix the permission; if no, stop the attempt. A plan that
' treated "permission denied" as one bug would either grant write access to the
' npm prefix or silence a hook someone asked for, and both are wrong.
'
' WHAT proveo COULD DO for case B, ranked by how little it assumes:
'   SAY SO EARLY. The seed already walks the workspace. A hook declared in
'     `.claude/settings.json` that is not executable is knowable before the run
'     starts, and a posture line beats a stop-hook error on every stop.
'   DO NOT chmod THE OPERATOR'S TREE. In direct mode that is their file on
'     their disk; silently changing its mode is the same class of overreach as
'     shredding a mounted `.env`.
'   CONSIDER CLONE MODE AS THE ANSWER. It already produces exec-correct,
'     runtime-owned files. If direct mode is the only broken case, the honest
'     advice may be "use a clone" rather than new machinery.
'
' ── WHAT IS NOT SETTLED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' WHETHER THE MESSAGE SHOULD VANISH OR BE REPLACED. Silencing the updater
' removes a line that, however useless, told the operator the version is fixed.
' A posture row saying so is better than a red ✘, but it is a different change
' and the def's `proveo.agent.version` label already carries the fact.
'
' WHETHER cecli NEEDS THE SAME. Its sample config sets `check-update: true`, and
' whether cecli's updater can write its venv at run time is UNMEASURED. Same
' class, different binary, and worth one probe before assuming.
title PLANNED — two permission denials reported every run,\nwith opposite remedies

component "the CLI\ninstalled as root at build" as CLI <<app>>
component "the run\nnon-root, hardened" as RUN <<app>>
component "**the npm prefix**\nunwritable, deliberately" as PREFIX <<error>>
component "✘ Auto-update failed\n· Run claude doctor" as MSG <<error>>

card "the fix" as FIX <<host>> {
  component """agentEnv:""\n""DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER: 1""" as ENV <<app>>
  component "a test that asserts it\nopencode already has one" as TEST <<app>>
}
component "**the wrong fix**\nmake the prefix writable" as WRONG <<error>>
component "the pinned version\n""CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION"" build-arg" as PIN <<app>>

CLI ARROW_MAIN RUN
RUN ARROW_ERROR PREFIX : the updater tries anyway
PREFIX ARROW_ERROR MSG
ENV ARROW_MAIN RUN : never tries, never fails
TEST ARROW_MAIN ENV : an unasserted env var\nis a comment
WRONG ARROW_ERROR PIN : a SUCCESSFUL update\nsilently unpins the image

note bottom of PREFIX
  **Working as designed.** Installed as root, run
  as non-root, ""proveo-harden"" applied and
  ""security.non-root=true"" asserted. Nothing
  grants the runtime user write access, and
  nothing should.
end note

note bottom of WRONG
  **A successful update is the worse outcome.**
  ""agent-version-pin"" exists so a run uses the
  version its image was built with. An updater
  that wins replaces that binary and the posture
  line naming the version becomes a lie.
end note

note bottom of ENV
  **The flag is already in the tree, mis-scoped.**
  ""defs/claudecode/mcp/Dockerfile"" sets
  ""DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1"" for a BUILD step only.
  The runtime ""agentEnv:"" carries two other
  variables and not this one.
end note

note right of MSG
  **And the advice is wrong here.** ""claude
  doctor"" is interactive; an unattended run has
  nobody to read it. The line costs a reader's
  attention on every single run.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Set it where the agent runs.** ""DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER: 1"" in claudecode's
  ""agentEnv:"", beside the two variables already there. One line, and the whole visible
  defect goes with it.
  --
  **2. Assert it**, the way ""defs/opencode/tests/test_security.sh"" asserts
  ""OPENCODE_AUTO_UPDATE"". An unasserted env var is a comment, and this class has already
  appeared three times in three defs.
  ==
  **Do NOT make the prefix writable.** It defeats the version pin, it lets the agent
  rewrite its own tooling mid-run against the hardened posture, and the container is
  ephemeral so a successful download is discarded at teardown anyway.
  --
  **Case B is the inverse, and that is the lesson.** A workspace ""\.claude/hooks"" script
  denied execution is a permission the operator WANTS granted — so the remedy is not
  silence but exec. proveo guarantees the bit for hooks it SHIPS (0755, image-baked,
  runtime-owned) and guarantees nothing for hooks the workspace brings.
  --
  **The rule**: ask whether the operator wants the thing to happen. If yes, fix the
  permission; if no, stop the attempt. Treating "permission denied" as one bug would
  either grant write access to the npm prefix or silence a hook somebody asked for.
  ==
  **Left open**: whether the removed line should be replaced by a posture row saying the
  version is fixed; whether cecli needs the same — its sample config sets
  ""check-update: true"" and whether its updater can write the venv is unmeasured; and
  whether case B is a proveo fault at all, since clone mode already produces
  exec-correct, runtime-owned files and only DIRECT mode carries the host's modes in.
end legend
@enduml
